{"zh":[{"start":3.25,"end":10.07,"text":"在火星稀薄的大气下面藏着一个谜：一片被流水塑造的荒漠地貌。"},{"start":10.09,"end":13.93,"text":"在遥远的过去，火星一定有过更温暖、更湿润的气候，"},{"start":13.95,"end":18.12,"text":"但科学家想知道：远古的火星到底有多湿？"},{"start":18.14,"end":24.68,"text":"在远古时期，我们有些迹象表明地表有水流过，但到底有多少水？"},{"start":24.7,"end":28.42,"text":"我们说的是海洋，还是小河、一点点雨？"},{"start":28.44,"end":32.83,"text":"所以行星上到底有多少水，这个定义非常模糊。"},{"start":32.85,"end":40.23,"text":"一个重大问题是：火星年轻时到底有多少水，又是怎样失去这些水的？"},{"start":40.25,"end":44.9,"text":"为了回答这个问题，NASA 戈达德太空飞行中心的一支研究团队"},{"start":44.92,"end":50.0,"text":"用地球上的红外望远镜研究火星大气中的水分子。"},{"start":50.02,"end":55.01,"text":"我们用了世界上三台主要的红外天文望远镜。"},{"start":55.03,"end":59.91,"text":"从地面上，我们其实一个晚上就能给这颗行星的整个半球拍一张快照。"},{"start":59.93,"end":67.83,"text":"新的红外地图揭示了火星不同地点、不同季节大气中普通水分子和重水分子的比例。"},{"start":67.85,"end":72.11,"text":"重水分子含有一种叫氘的氢的重同位素，"},{"start":72.13,"end":77.16,"text":"它被困在火星的水循环里，而普通的氢则流失到太空。"},{"start":77.18,"end":81.63,"text":"研究人员发现，极地冰盖里的水氘含量非常高，"},{"start":81.65,"end":85.33,"text":"说明火星失去了极大量的水。"},{"start":85.35,"end":93.33,"text":"现在我们知道，火星水中重水，也就是氘化的水，比地球海水富集得多。"},{"start":93.35,"end":98.91,"text":"这马上让我们能估算火星年轻时以来失去了多少水。"},{"start":98.93,"end":106.25,"text":"结果表明，远古海洋今天只剩下 13% 留在这颗行星上，储存在极地冰盖里。"},{"start":106.27,"end":113.38,"text":"这片海洋的 87% 已经流失到太空。这意味着早期的火星和今天看起来大不一样，"},{"start":113.4,"end":116.88,"text":"表面有相当大一部分被水覆盖。"},{"start":116.9,"end":122.98,"text":"所以真正有趣的问题是：它能形成一片海吗？答案是可以。"},{"start":123.0,"end":127.42,"text":"在北部平原，那里相对平坦，但比行星其他地方低，"},{"start":127.44,"end":134.33,"text":"会形成一片大约占行星表面积 20% 的海洋。"},{"start":134.35,"end":137.08,"text":"所以那是相当可观的海洋。"},{"start":148.55,"end":152.25,"text":"研究人员把火星地形和新估算的水流失量结合起来，"},{"start":152.27,"end":157.38,"text":"模拟出了火星远古的海洋，以及它逃逸到太空的过程。"},{"start":157.4,"end":163.66,"text":"在几十亿年里，火星失去了大气，也失去了让水保持液态所需的压力和热量，"},{"start":163.68,"end":166.76,"text":"海洋因此缩小，向北退去。"},{"start":166.78,"end":174.6,"text":"剩下的水最终凝结冻在南北两极，形成了我们今天看到的火星冰盖。"},{"start":174.62,"end":181.53,"text":"这个新情景意味着火星保持湿润的时间比以前以为的更长，宜居的时期也就更长。"},{"start":181.55,"end":188.78,"text":"我们现在知道，火星湿润的时间比我们以前以为的长得多。"},{"start":188.8,"end":193.18,"text":"好奇号显示它湿润了十五亿年，已经远远长于"},{"start":193.2,"end":196.88,"text":"地球上生命发展所需的时间，"},{"start":196.9,"end":200.98,"text":"而现在我们看到，火星湿润的时期一定还要更长。"}],"de":[],"en":[{"start":3.25,"end":10.07,"text":"Beneath the thin atmosphere of Mars lies an enigma: a desert landscape shaped by flowing water.","words":[["Beneath","在…下面"],["the","这"],["thin","稀薄"],["atmosphere","大气"],["of","的"],["Mars","火星"],["lies","躺着"],["an","一个"],["enigma:","谜"],["a","一片"],["desert","荒漠"],["landscape","地貌"],["shaped","塑造"],["by","被"],["flowing","流动"],["water.","水"]]},{"start":10.09,"end":13.93,"text":"In the distant past, Mars must have had a warmer, wetter climate,","words":[["In","在"],["the","这"],["distant","遥远"],["past,","过去"],["Mars","火星"],["must","一定"],["have","有"],["had","有过"],["a","一个"],["warmer,","更暖"],["wetter","更湿"],["climate,","气候"]]},{"start":13.95,"end":18.12,"text":"but scientists wonder: just how wet was ancient Mars?","words":[["but","但"],["scientists","科学家"],["wonder:","想知道"],["just","到底"],["how","多"],["wet","湿"],["was","曾"],["ancient","远古"],["Mars?","火星"]]},{"start":18.14,"end":24.68,"text":"So in the ancient past, we have some indications that water was flowing on the surface, but how much water was there?","words":[["So","所以"],["in","在"],["the","这"],["ancient","远古"],["past,","过去"],["we","我们"],["have","有"],["some","一些"],["indications","迹象"],["that","那"],["water","水"],["was","曾"],["flowing","流动"],["on","在"],["the","这"],["surface,","表面"],["but","但"],["how","多"],["much","多少"],["water","水"],["was","曾"],["there?","有"]]},{"start":24.7,"end":28.42,"text":"Are we talking about oceans, are we talking about small rivers, a little rain?","words":[["Are","是"],["we","我们"],["talking","谈论"],["about","关于"],["oceans,","海洋"],["are","是"],["we","我们"],["talking","谈论"],["about","关于"],["small","小"],["rivers,","河"],["a","一"],["little","点"],["rain?","雨"]]},{"start":28.44,"end":32.83,"text":"So these definitions of how much water was on the planet was very undefined.","words":[["So","所以"],["these","这些"],["definitions","定义"],["of","的"],["how","多"],["much","多少"],["water","水"],["was","曾"],["on","在"],["the","这"],["planet","行星"],["was","曾"],["very","非常"],["undefined.","不明确"]]},{"start":32.85,"end":40.23,"text":"A major question has been: how much water did Mars actually have when it was young, and how did it lose that water?","words":[["A","一个"],["major","重大"],["question","问题"],["has","已"],["been:","是"],["how","多"],["much","多少"],["water","水"],["did","曾"],["Mars","火星"],["actually","实际"],["have","有"],["when","当"],["it","它"],["was","曾"],["young,","年轻"],["and","和"],["how","怎样"],["did","曾"],["it","它"],["lose","失去"],["that","那"],["water?","水"]]},{"start":40.25,"end":44.9,"text":"To answer this question, a team of researchers at NASA's Goddard Space Flight Center","words":[["To","为了"],["answer","回答"],["this","这个"],["question,","问题"],["a","一支"],["team","团队"],["of","的"],["researchers","研究人员"],["at","在"],["NASA's","NASA的"],["Goddard","戈达德"],["Space","太空"],["Flight","飞行"],["Center","中心"]]},{"start":44.92,"end":50.0,"text":"used infrared telescopes on Earth to study water molecules in the Martian atmosphere.","words":[["used","用了"],["infrared","红外"],["telescopes","望远镜"],["on","在"],["Earth","地球"],["to","去"],["study","研究"],["water","水"],["molecules","分子"],["in","在"],["the","这"],["Martian","火星"],["atmosphere.","大气"]]},{"start":50.02,"end":55.01,"text":"We used the world's three major telescopes for infrared astronomy.","words":[["We","我们"],["used","用了"],["the","这"],["world's","世界的"],["three","三台"],["major","主要"],["telescopes","望远镜"],["for","为"],["infrared","红外"],["astronomy.","天文学"]]},{"start":55.03,"end":59.91,"text":"From the ground we could actually take a snapshot of the whole hemisphere of the planet on a single night.","words":[["From","从"],["the","这"],["ground","地面"],["we","我们"],["could","能"],["actually","其实"],["take","拍"],["a","一张"],["snapshot","快照"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["whole","整个"],["hemisphere","半球"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["planet","行星"],["on","在"],["a","一个"],["single","单个"],["night.","晚上"]]},{"start":59.93,"end":67.83,"text":"The new infrared maps reveal the atmospheric ratio of normal to heavy water molecules at different locations and seasons on Mars.","words":[["The","这"],["new","新"],["infrared","红外"],["maps","地图"],["reveal","揭示"],["the","这"],["atmospheric","大气的"],["ratio","比例"],["of","的"],["normal","普通"],["to","对"],["heavy","重"],["water","水"],["molecules","分子"],["at","在"],["different","不同"],["locations","地点"],["and","和"],["seasons","季节"],["on","在"],["Mars.","火星"]]},{"start":67.85,"end":72.11,"text":"Heavy water molecules contain a heavy isotope of hydrogen called deuterium,","words":[["Heavy","重"],["water","水"],["molecules","分子"],["contain","含有"],["a","一种"],["heavy","重"],["isotope","同位素"],["of","的"],["hydrogen","氢"],["called","叫做"],["deuterium,","氘"]]},{"start":72.13,"end":77.16,"text":"which remains trapped in the Martian water cycle while normal hydrogen is lost to space.","words":[["which","它"],["remains","保持"],["trapped","被困"],["in","在"],["the","这"],["Martian","火星"],["water","水"],["cycle","循环"],["while","而"],["normal","普通"],["hydrogen","氢"],["is","是"],["lost","流失"],["to","到"],["space.","太空"]]},{"start":77.18,"end":81.63,"text":"The researchers found that water from the polar ice caps is highly enriched in deuterium,","words":[["The","这"],["researchers","研究人员"],["found","发现"],["that","那"],["water","水"],["from","来自"],["the","这"],["polar","极地"],["ice","冰"],["caps","盖"],["is","是"],["highly","高度"],["enriched","富集"],["in","在"],["deuterium,","氘"]]},{"start":81.65,"end":85.33,"text":"indicating that Mars has lost a tremendous quantity of water.","words":[["indicating","表明"],["that","那"],["Mars","火星"],["has","已"],["lost","失去"],["a","一个"],["tremendous","极大的"],["quantity","量"],["of","的"],["water.","水"]]},{"start":85.35,"end":93.33,"text":"Now we know that Mars water is much more enriched than terrestrial ocean water in the heavy form of water, the deuterated form.","words":[["Now","现在"],["we","我们"],["know","知道"],["that","那"],["Mars","火星"],["water","水"],["is","是"],["much","很"],["more","更"],["enriched","富集"],["than","比"],["terrestrial","地球"],["ocean","海洋"],["water","水"],["in","在"],["the","这"],["heavy","重"],["form","形式"],["of","的"],["water,","水"],["the","这"],["deuterated","氘化的"],["form.","形式"]]},{"start":93.35,"end":98.91,"text":"Immediately that permits us to estimate the amount of water Mars has lost since it was young.","words":[["Immediately","立即"],["that","那"],["permits","允许"],["us","我们"],["to","去"],["estimate","估算"],["the","这"],["amount","量"],["of","的"],["water","水"],["Mars","火星"],["has","已"],["lost","失去"],["since","自从"],["it","它"],["was","曾"],["young.","年轻"]]},{"start":98.93,"end":106.25,"text":"The findings indicate that only 13% of an ancient ocean remains on the planet today, now stored in the polar ice caps.","words":[["The","这"],["findings","结果"],["indicate","表明"],["that","那"],["only","只"],["13%","13%"],["of","的"],["an","一个"],["ancient","远古"],["ocean","海洋"],["remains","留存"],["on","在"],["the","这"],["planet","行星"],["today,","今天"],["now","现在"],["stored","储存"],["in","在"],["the","这"],["polar","极地"],["ice","冰"],["caps.","盖"]]},{"start":106.27,"end":113.38,"text":"87% of this ocean has been lost to space. This means that early Mars would have looked much different than it does today,","words":[["87%","87%"],["of","的"],["this","这个"],["ocean","海洋"],["has","已"],["been","被"],["lost","流失"],["to","到"],["space.","太空"],["This","这"],["means","意味着"],["that","那"],["early","早期"],["Mars","火星"],["would","会"],["have","有"],["looked","看起来"],["much","很"],["different","不同"],["than","比"],["it","它"],["does","是"],["today,","今天"]]},{"start":113.4,"end":116.88,"text":"with a significant portion of its surface covered by water.","words":[["with","以"],["a","一个"],["significant","相当大"],["portion","部分"],["of","的"],["its","它的"],["surface","表面"],["covered","覆盖"],["by","被"],["water.","水"]]},{"start":116.9,"end":122.98,"text":"So the really interesting question is, could it form a sea or an ocean? And indeed, it would.","words":[["So","所以"],["the","这"],["really","真正"],["interesting","有趣的"],["question","问题"],["is,","是"],["could","能"],["it","它"],["form","形成"],["a","一片"],["sea","海"],["or","或"],["an","一个"],["ocean?","海洋"],["And","而"],["indeed,","确实"],["it","它"],["would.","会"]]},{"start":123.0,"end":127.42,"text":"In the northern plains, which is a relatively flat region but depressed from the rest of the planet,","words":[["In","在"],["the","这"],["northern","北部"],["plains,","平原"],["which","那"],["is","是"],["a","一个"],["relatively","相对"],["flat","平坦"],["region","区域"],["but","但"],["depressed","低洼"],["from","比"],["the","这"],["rest","其余"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["planet,","行星"]]},{"start":127.44,"end":134.33,"text":"it would form an ocean that was approximately 20% of the planet's surface area.","words":[["it","它"],["would","会"],["form","形成"],["an","一个"],["ocean","海洋"],["that","那"],["was","曾"],["approximately","大约"],["20%","20%"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["planet's","行星的"],["surface","表面"],["area.","面积"]]},{"start":134.35,"end":137.08,"text":"And so that is a respectable ocean.","words":[["And","而"],["so","所以"],["that","那"],["is","是"],["a","一个"],["respectable","可观的"],["ocean.","海洋"]]},{"start":148.55,"end":152.25,"text":"By combining Martian topography with the new estimate for water loss,","words":[["By","通过"],["combining","结合"],["Martian","火星"],["topography","地形"],["with","与"],["the","这"],["new","新"],["estimate","估算"],["for","为"],["water","水"],["loss,","流失"]]},{"start":152.27,"end":157.38,"text":"the researchers were able to simulate Mars' ancient ocean, and its escape to space.","words":[["the","这"],["researchers","研究人员"],["were","曾"],["able","能够"],["to","去"],["simulate","模拟"],["Mars'","火星"],["ancient","远古"],["ocean,","海洋"],["and","和"],["its","它的"],["escape","逃逸"],["to","到"],["space.","太空"]]},{"start":157.4,"end":163.66,"text":"As Mars lost its atmosphere over billions of years, it lost the pressure and heat needed to keep water liquid,","words":[["As","随着"],["Mars","火星"],["lost","失去"],["its","它的"],["atmosphere","大气"],["over","在"],["billions","数十亿"],["of","的"],["years,","年"],["it","它"],["lost","失去"],["the","这"],["pressure","压力"],["and","和"],["heat","热"],["needed","需要"],["to","去"],["keep","保持"],["water","水"],["liquid,","液态"]]},{"start":163.68,"end":166.76,"text":"causing the ocean to shrink and recede northward.","words":[["causing","导致"],["the","这"],["ocean","海洋"],["to","去"],["shrink","缩小"],["and","和"],["recede","退"],["northward.","向北"]]},{"start":166.78,"end":174.6,"text":"The remaining water eventually condensed and froze over the north and south poles, giving Mars the ice caps that we see today.","words":[["The","这"],["remaining","剩下的"],["water","水"],["eventually","最终"],["condensed","凝结"],["and","和"],["froze","冻结"],["over","在"],["the","这"],["north","北"],["and","和"],["south","南"],["poles,","极"],["giving","给"],["Mars","火星"],["the","这"],["ice","冰"],["caps","盖"],["that","那"],["we","我们"],["see","看到"],["today.","今天"]]},{"start":174.62,"end":181.53,"text":"This new scenario means that Mars would have stayed wet for longer than previously thought, expanding its ancient habitability.","words":[["This","这个"],["new","新"],["scenario","情景"],["means","意味着"],["that","那"],["Mars","火星"],["would","会"],["have","有"],["stayed","保持"],["wet","湿润"],["for","达"],["longer","更长"],["than","比"],["previously","以前"],["thought,","认为"],["expanding","扩大"],["its","它的"],["ancient","远古"],["habitability.","宜居性"]]},{"start":181.55,"end":188.78,"text":"We now know that Mars was wet for a much longer time than we thought before.","words":[["We","我们"],["now","现在"],["know","知道"],["that","那"],["Mars","火星"],["was","曾"],["wet","湿润"],["for","达"],["a","一个"],["much","很"],["longer","更长"],["time","时间"],["than","比"],["we","我们"],["thought","认为"],["before.","以前"]]},{"start":188.8,"end":193.18,"text":"Curiosity shows it was wet for one-and-a-half-billion years, already much longer","words":[["Curiosity","好奇号"],["shows","显示"],["it","它"],["was","曾"],["wet","湿润"],["for","达"],["one-and-a-half-billion","十五亿"],["years,","年"],["already","已经"],["much","很"],["longer","更长"]]},{"start":193.2,"end":196.88,"text":"than the period of time needed for life to develop on Earth,","words":[["than","比"],["the","这"],["period","时期"],["of","的"],["time","时间"],["needed","需要"],["for","为"],["life","生命"],["to","去"],["develop","发展"],["on","在"],["Earth,","地球"]]},{"start":196.9,"end":200.98,"text":"and now we see that Mars must have been wet for a period even longer.","words":[["and","而"],["now","现在"],["we","我们"],["see","看到"],["that","那"],["Mars","火星"],["must","一定"],["have","有"],["been","是"],["wet","湿润"],["for","达"],["a","一个"],["period","时期"],["even","甚至"],["longer.","更长"]]}]}